  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Uburezi Iwacu</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Rwanda):  ..USAID will use FY 2022 funds to.implement the Uburezi Iwacu (Homes and Communities) activity. The activity will.improve literacy outcomes for all Rwandan children by increasing their.engagement in stimulating home and community environments and supporting the.development of literacy skills. This will be achieved by increasing active.engagement among parents and children, increasing access to reading materials in.children&apos;s homes, and expanding opportunities for language development and.reading practice outside school. The activity will include support to increase.the participation of children with disabilities in community literacy.activities, improve parents&apos; skills to support the development of their.children with disabilities, and increase the enrollment and retention of.children with disabilities. Interventions may include institutionalization of.community reading clubs for children, provision of books to community libraries.and librarian training, and training of caregivers at community-based early.childhood development centers.. .Uburezi Iwacu will help the Government of Rwanda develop the human and institutional capacity necessary to sustain improved learning outcomes. As improved literacy skills in the early grades of primary school directly contribute to children&apos;s success and retention in the education system and their future employment, the activity will contribute to Rwanda&apos;s long-term ability to participate in the global economy, including trade with the United States, by building an educated population.. .By improving basic education service delivery and increasing institutional capacity to deliver those services, this activity will contribute to USAID Country Development Cooperation Strategy Development Objective 2: &quot;Improved learning outcomes.&quot;......</narrative>
  </description>
